---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, AUTHOR, MAIN_SITE } from '../config';

// Kept current automatically so the "last updated" line never goes stale.
const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${SITE.url}/legal#page`,
    name: `Legal — ${SITE.title}`,
    description: `Terms of use, copyright, code sample licensing, and disclaimers for ${SITE.title}.`,
    about: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#person` },
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal"
  description={`Terms of use, copyright, code sample licensing and disclaimers for ${SITE.title}.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Terms &amp; Legal Notices</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-reading mt-10 max-w-none">
      <p>
        These terms cover your use of <strong>{SITE.title}</strong> at
        <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>, a personal publication written and run by
        {AUTHOR.name}. By reading, downloading, or otherwise using anything on this site,
        you accept what is set out below. How your data is handled is covered separately
        on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Whose views these are</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is written in a personal capacity. The articles, code samples,
        and opinions are my own, and they do not represent the views, positions, or
        strategy of any employer, client, or organisation I am associated with.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Nothing published here is produced on behalf of an employer or as part of any
          commercial engagement.
        </li>
        <li>
          No confidential, proprietary, internal, or company-owned information, code, or
          data appears on this site.
        </li>
        <li>
          Products and platforms are written about from public documentation and my own
          hands-on use, never from privileged access.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Copyright</h2>
      <p>
        All articles, short videos, images, diagrams, and other written material on this
        site are &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} {AUTHOR.name}, all rights reserved.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are welcome to quote a short extract for review, commentary, or teaching, as
        long as you attribute it to {AUTHOR.name} and link back to the original article.
        Republishing a full article, translating it, or reposting it on another site —
        including feeding it into a mirror or content farm — is not permitted without
        written permission. Ask first via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Code samples</h2>
      <p>
        Code published in articles exists to explain an idea. Unless an article says
        otherwise, you may use, adapt, and ship the snippets in your own projects freely
        and without attribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        The samples are provided <strong>as is</strong>, without warranty of any kind.
        They are written for clarity rather than production hardening, so review,
        test, and secure anything you take from here before it reaches real users or
        real data.
      </p>

      <h2>No professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Articles here are technical notes and opinions, not professional advice for your
        specific situation. Architecture, security, licensing, and cost decisions depend
        on context I cannot see from here. You remain responsible for validating any
        approach against your own requirements, and for any outcome of acting on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and availability</h2>
      <p>
        Cloud platforms, SDKs, and AI tooling change constantly. An article reflects what
        was accurate when it was published or last updated — versions, pricing, portal
        screens, and APIs may have moved since. I correct errors when I find them, but I
        make no guarantee that every page is current, complete, or uninterrupted.
      </p>

      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Microsoft, Azure, GitHub, Google, Firebase, Flutter, and all other product and
        company names referenced on this site are the trademarks of their respective
        owners. They are used descriptively, for identification and educational purposes
        only. Their use here does not imply any endorsement of, affiliation with, or
        sponsorship of this site by those owners.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site carries ads served by Google AdSense, which help cover its running
        costs. Ads are selected by the ad network, not by me, and their appearance beside
        an article is not a recommendation of the advertised product. The cookies
        involved are described on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What you submit</h2>
      <p>
        Some parts of the site accept input from readers — the contact form, comments,
        reactions, testimonials, and event registration. By submitting something you
        confirm it is yours to share, and you give me permission to display it on the
        site where that is the obvious purpose, such as a testimonial or a comment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not submit confidential material, credentials, or anyone else's
        personal information. I may edit or remove any submission that is unlawful,
        abusive, off-topic, or spam.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You may read, link to, and share this site freely. You may not attempt to break
        into or disrupt it, scrape it at a volume that degrades it for other readers, or
        reuse its content in bulk to train or populate another publication or model.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link out to documentation, repositories, and other sites. Those are not
        under my control, and a link is not an endorsement of the destination's content,
        terms, or privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {AUTHOR.name} is not liable for any loss
        or damage arising from your use of this site or anything published on it,
        including any code sample or linked resource.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections and takedown requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe something here is factually wrong, infringes your copyright, or
        should not be published, tell me through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
        with enough detail to identify the page. Genuine issues get fixed or removed
        quickly.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated from time to time. Changes are posted on this page
        with a revised "last updated" date above, and continuing to use the site means
        you accept the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about anything on this page, or about {MAIN_SITE.label}? Reach out
        through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
